### 3. How Tool Calls Are Currently Displayed

Tool calls are displayed as **static lines** in the `displayLines` array, using ANSI-labeled prefixes:

| Tool            | Display                                                                 | Label Function     |
| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ |
| `query_nba_db`    | `[SQL] SELECT * FROM ...` (full SQL) + `[SQL] ⠋ Running query...` (spinner) | `sqlLabel()` (cyan)  |
| `get_schema_info` | `[SQL] ⠋ Looking up schema...`                                            | `sqlLabel()` (cyan)  |
| Other tools     | `⠋ Running {name}...`                                                     | `statusText()` (dim) |
| Tool error      | `[Error] Tool {name} failed: {error}`                                     | `errorLabel()` (red) |

**Problems/inconsistencies:**
- Tool **end** events do NOT update the display -- the spinner line from `tool_start` remains forever (it is never removed or replaced). The spinner frame is only recalculated when `handleTokenEvent` fires (via `getSpinnerFrame(this.spinnerTick, ...)`) which happens on token events, not tool end events.
- For `get_schema_info`, only a spinner line is shown (no SQL to display).
- The `tool_end` output is discarded from the UI entirely -- users never see what the tool returned.
- `activeToolCount` tracks how many tools are "in flight" but is only used in `handleTokenEvent` to decide whether to push a new `[AI] ` line.

