### Summary of Key Architectural Observations

| Aspect            | Current State                                                                                                                                                                           |
| ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **Streaming**         | Works via LangGraph v2 `streamEvents`. Yields tokens, tool_start/end/error, chain_stage, usage, done, error. Token streaming works properly for LLM text output.                          |
| **Tool call display** | Static lines -- `[SQL]` label for DB queries, spinner for schema, dim text for others. **Tool output is never shown to the user.** The spinner from `tool_start` is never removed on `tool_end`.  |
| **Message rendering** | Lines stored in `string[]`, joined with `\n\n`, converted through `markdownToAnsi()` then `ansiToStyledText()`. Final rendering in `renderDisplay()` adds separators between user turns.          |
| **Graph**             | 6-node StateGraph with SQL critic loop (max 3 retries), hallucination detection (max 2 retries), intent classification, schema injection. Uses `Command` for dynamic routing.             |
| **LLM integration**   | `ChatOpenAI` pointed at OpenRouter. Temperature 0.3, 120s timeout, `parallel_tool_calls: true`. Dynamic model selection via `MODEL` env var or interactive picker.                            |
| **System prompt**     | Dynamically built from live DB schema -- lists all tables, columns for core tables, detailed SQL cookbook, source priority, anti-hallucination rules. ~248 lines.                       |
| **Largest gap**       | Tool output is invisible to users; tool-end spinner artifacts persist. The UI treats tool calls as transient "in-progress" indicators rather than displaying what the agent discovered. |
